    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0923" n="883" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg883"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/1–2252: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 389<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the United States
                        Delegation at the United Nations General Assembly (Roosevelt) to the
                        Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-01-22T22:00:00+01:00">January 22, 1952—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Delga 1142. For Hickerson (UNA) from Gross. Re: Suez. Eban (Israel) on instrs
                    from Tel Aviv said his govt is increasingly restless <pb facs="0924" n="884"
                        xml:id="pg884"/> about inactivity SC on Suez res.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d389-f1"/> It fears world attention re Suez is focused so much on
                    Anglo-Egypt relations that Israel’s interests in unmolested transit is becoming
                    forgotten. Eban has talked along same line to Jebb. I gather this is first
                    warning of possible Israeli plan to present at Suez ports cargoes or ships
                    openly destined for Israel. If transit refused, Israel would probably raise
                    matter in SC, seeking SC steps to obtain compliance with Sept 1 SC res.</p>
                <p>Does Dept want me to talk with Jebb, and if so along what line?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d389-f1" n="1" xml:id="d389-f1-content">
                <p>Reference is to the resolution adopted by the Security Council on Sept. 1, 1951
                    calling upon Egypt to terminate restrictions on the passage of international
                    shipping through the Suez Canal (U.N. doc. S/2322); for text, see <ref
                        target="frus1951v05#pg_848"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1951, vol. V, p. 848</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
